Name: qubes-buskill-vm
Version: @VERSION@
Release: @REL@%{?dist}

Summary: Qubes BusKill package for VM
License: GPLv2+
URL: https://www.buskill.in/

Source0: %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz

BuildArch: noarch
BuildRequires: make
BuildRequires: systemd-rpm-macros

%description
BusKill is a dead man's switch designed to protect your computer if it is
physically seized. You connect one end of a USB cable to your laptop and attach
the other end to your body (e.g. a belt loop). If someone snatches your laptop
and runs, the cable disconnects and BusKill automatically triggers a security
response: locking the screen, rebooting, or destroying encryption keys, before
an attacker can access your data.

For more information about BusKill, visit https://www.buskill.in/.

This package contains files for TemplateVMs (the USB qube and interface qubes):
the BusKill service, udev rules, and trigger scripts

%prep
%setup -q

%install
make install-vm DESTDIR=$RPM_BUILD_ROOT SYSLIBDIR=/usr/lib

%post
%systemd_post buskill.service

%preun
%systemd_preun buskill.service

%postun
%systemd_postun_with_restart buskill.service

%files
/etc/buskill/buskill.lock.rules
/etc/buskill/buskill.rules
/etc/qubes-rpc/buskill.Disarm
/etc/qubes/rpc-config/buskill.Disarm
/etc/qubes-rpc/qubes.LockScreen
/usr/bin/buskill-disarm.sh
/usr/bin/buskill-lock-interface-qubes.sh
/usr/lib/systemd/system-preset/80-buskill.preset
/usr/lib/systemd/system/buskill.service
/usr/share/applications/buskill-disarm.desktop

%changelog
@CHANGELOG@
